The stub predicate has one definition: TypeDefinition.isStub, referenced by TypeLoader, Completeness, DomainBuilder and the scripts (closes #47)

Dev accepted, in the words "Accepted, build it", the design-point recommendation brought after the #50 close.
OWNING ISSUE: https://github.com/ejb816/nexonix/issues/47, "Promote isStub to a shared main-tree predicate" — its
November 4 status comment names the remaining scope as consolidation against current callers, not the restoration of
the old three-site design, and that is what this commit does. With it the issue has no remaining scope.

WHY. The invariant "a definition with all four role and structure aspects empty is a stub — declared, not authored"
was spelled in five places and owned by none: TypeLoader.isStub (by name: load, then the four tests inline),
DomainBuilder.isStub in the mods tier (by definition, the same four lines; four internal sites, eleven test sites),
Completeness's rule (the same four tests as four `con` lines, four `where` clauses), and six scripts (the same test
negated by hand as "loaded"). DerivationResolvable, which the issue named in July, no longer carries it; it tests
ontology membership since 2026-10-09.

THE DESIGN POINT, accepted: the one definition lives on TypeDefinition itself, as the global
`fix isStub (TypeDefinition -> Boolean)` with a lambda value — exactly the form DracoAspect.isEmpty and
DomainAspect.isEmpty already take, the type that owns the shape owning the test of it; in Haskell
`isStub :: TypeDefinition -> Bool` in the TypeDefinition module. REJECTED: naming it isEmpty to match the aspects (a stub
has a name and may carry a record, and "stub" is the word every caller and DRACO.md use); defining it as equality with
`TypeDefinition(td.typeName)` (it would reclassify a definition carrying only a codec aspect or a `uses` record, a
semantic change the issue does not ask for). Semantics are unchanged: the four-aspect conjunction, codec aspect and
record ignored, as every site had it; both stub shapes the system makes — the loader's typeName-only stub and the
dictionary's placeholder, each `TypeDefinition(name)` — satisfy it.

BUILT. TypeDefinition.drake gains a `globals` section with the one line; TypeLoader.drake's isStub body is
`TypeDefinition.isStub(loadType(typeName))`, the by-name convenience the engine calls at its two codec-eligibility
sites kept, its `loc` gone; Completeness.drake's four conditions are one, `con TypeDefinition.isStub(td)`. The three
JSON are `DrakeCLI parse` of their surfaces and the three Scala `GeneratorCLI generate` of the JSON, on the compiled
engine of d026cd3 (no engine change, so no two-run protocol): TypeDefinition's companion gains `lazy val isStub:
TypeDefinition => Boolean`, TypeLoader's isStub is one line, Completeness renders one `w0` and one `where`.
DomainBuilder.isStub is removed and its three internal sites say TypeDefinition.isStub; so do the eleven test sites
(ExampleLoadingTest, CompletenessRulesTest, MinimalTypeTest, DomainLoadingTest ×2, EditorTest ×2,
DerivationResolvableRulesTest, DreamsTest ×3) and the six scripts (inspect-type, list-domain, diff-type,
derivation-chain, who-extends, list-domains), whose "loaded" is `!TypeDefinition.isStub(td)`. `grep DomainBuilder.isStub`
over src finds nothing. TypeDefinitionTest +1: a bare name is a stub, Null is a stub, a record alone does not authorize,
